[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352445316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111072#issuecomment-3352445316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111072","id":3352445316,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H0kGE","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T14:21:16Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:21:16Z","body":"Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/86172\r\n\r\nAs stated over there, I agree with the approach of handling `GET_NODE` in `_guess_expression_type`. However, when we do this, we have to remove the `_get_subscript_type` codepath at the same time, to prevent code duplication, to keep the number of codepaths low and to ensure, that the new code handles all edge cases correctly. (There are quite a lot of test cases for get node completion and they would all take the old codepath at the moment. Ideally the new codepath should pass all those tests as well.)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352445316/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352487031","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111072#issuecomment-3352487031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111072","id":3352487031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H0uR3","user":{"login":"Macksaur","id":86566939,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NTY2OTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86566939?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur","html_url":"https://github.com/Macksaur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Macksaur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T14:28:56Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T14:28:56Z","body":"Oh? This has already been discussed! I will take a look at the prior discussion.\r\n\r\nSaying that though, I am a fan of incremental work. There is a lot to get right with a \"complete\" solution, however this knocks one more edge-case out where autocomplete fails. There's even a test!\r\n\r\nIt's funny, originally I tried to unify the `_get_subscript_type` codepath myself too! ...but it actually contains a lot of mixed type / parameter spaghetti if you do that. You're welcome to try and untangle it. Once the unified method started creeping down the page, I just deleted it. I would rather fix this today; more complex PRs never get a serious shake.\r\n\r\nIf you want a more comprehensive refactor at some point in the future, consider using this as a stepping stone and a validation point.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3352487031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]